WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.835
In this lesson, you will learn to use broadcasts and variables to add a start screen, levels and a game-over state to a game.

2
00:00:12.435 --> 00:00:19.757
A game is in different states: a start menu, playing, the next level, game over.

3
00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:24.470
Code needs to know which state it is in.

4
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:30.217
When the player presses space on the menu, broadcast start.

5
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:36.235
Every sprite that needs to begin listens for “when I receive start”.

6
00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:41.548
A level variable remembers how far the player is.

7
00:00:41.548 --> 00:00:49.304
When the score reaches a target, change the level, switch the backdrop and make it harder.

8
00:00:49.904 --> 00:00:58.530
When lives reach 0 or time runs out, broadcast game over: show the final score and stop all.

9
00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:02.974
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

10
00:01:02.974 --> 00:01:08.122
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
